  "text": "Why do rich people get richer? The answer is compound interest. Imagine you save $100 at 10 % a year. After one year you have $110. The next year you earn interest on $110, not on $100. After 10 years your $100 becomes $259, without adding a single cent. After 30 years it becomes $1 ,745. That is the power of time. Start early, even with a small amount, and let your money work while you sleep.",
